    "created_at": "2022-10-10T20:01:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-10T20:01:02Z",
    "body": "Given that we've already shipped by defaulting to index 0, I don't think we should change that default. Unlike the change to all-sync SyncAccessHandles, which is technically not backwards-compatible but which we expect will be a no-op for virtually all uses, changing the default here would be a silent behavioral change. \r\n\r\nHowever, this seems like a reasonable thing to allow developers to opt into. Something like `{ at: 'cursor' }`?\r\n\r\n\"Seek\" would be achievable by writing zero zero bytes at a given offset. But that raises the question of whether we need the equivalent of Posix's `SEEK_CUR`: a way to seek to an offset from the cursor. Conceptually, `{ at: 'cursor' + 10 }`",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
